s_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-27T18:06:12Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "https://x.com/__scottsaunders/status/2048671826541195439?s=61&t=6R_oHPgOGUbhTkugPCY0SA", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-27T18:06:15Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Yaar, ye Mumtaz Mahal toh poori Aishwarya Rai lag rahi hai", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-27T18:06:18Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "One of the agenda items for the 1852 Territorial Legislature in this part of the United States was deciding the territorial boundaries for the county around the fledgling communities in the X and Y area. The legislature finally chose the name Z County, after then Vice President elect William Rufus  Z. One year later, ‘A’ county was created out of the southern part of Z county. ‘A’ was chosen for the then US President, B A. The denizens of the city X and Z county understandably resented the association with Z, who was a slave owner and a staunch advocate of slavery. In the 1980s, renaming efforts thus came to a head. The fact that Z shared a last name with C was fortuitous as it enabled renaming at minimal logistical and practical expense. An informal motion renaming Z county after C was adopted in 1986, and formalized in state law in 2005. The 2005 law also approved the change of logo from the ‘imperial crown’ to an image of C. ID X, Y, Z, A, B, C.", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-27T18:06:22Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Was thinking of putting one around sealing the league title last year on this day 😂\nBut time zone k chakar mein 26-7 ho gya uska 😂", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-27T18:07:14Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Jamestown", "role": "chat", "is_correct": nul